=== exact (sympy): R3^2 = 1/3, R5^2 = (5-sqrt5)/10, chord_m = 1 ===
R3 simplifies to sqrt(3)/3 ; R3^2 = 1/3
R5^2 - (5-sqrt5)/10 = 0 (numeric residual at 60 digits: -0.e-191 )
cos(pi/10)^2 = (5+sqrt5)/8 -> R5^2 = 1/(4cos^2) = 2/(5+sqrt5) = (5-sqrt5)/10 : exact
sin(pi m/n) = cos(pi/(2n)) for n=2m+1 (n=3,5,7,9 checked exactly)
=== L7 identities used in the arc/vertex support-function proof (sympy, exact) ===
2 sin(a-delta) cos(delta) - sin a - sin(a-2 delta) = 0
2 sin(a+delta) cos(delta) - sin a - sin(a+2 delta) = 0
=== L4: sum_j |p-V_j|^2 = n|p|^2 + n R^2 for regular n-gon (n=3,5) ===
n=3: sum - (n|p|^2+nR^2) = 0
n=5: sum - (n|p|^2+nR^2) = 0
=== L5: |R_rho V - R_rho' V| = 2R |sin((rho-rho')/2)| ===
chord^2 - 4R^2 sin^2((rho1-rho2)/2) = 0
